        answer: "The complete field record: the EOR's structural observation reports from each milestone visit, all special inspection reports with every deficiency dispositioned, the approved deferred submittals with confirmation of installation per the approvals, material test reports where the design required them, and the final site review documentation. I assemble this record as the project proceeds — not at closeout — because reconstructing a field record after the fact is unreliable. The certification letter references the record specifically: visits dated, reports reviewed, dispositions documented. That traceability is what makes the letter credible to the AHJ and what makes it a professional statement rather than a formality.",
